{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,24]],"date-time":"2026-04-24T12:17:05Z","timestamp":1777033025806,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":42,"publisher":"American Mathematical Society (AMS)","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2017,12,22]],"date-time":"2017-12-22T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1513900800000},"content-version":"am","delay-in-days":365,"URL":"https://www.ams.org/publications/copyright-and-permissions"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Trans. Amer. Math. Soc."],"abstract":"<p>\n                    Let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left-parenthesis z right-parenthesis equals sigma-summation Underscript n equals 1 Overscript normal infinity Endscripts a Subscript f Baseline left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis q Superscript n Baseline element-of upper S Subscript k Superscript new Baseline left-parenthesis normal upper Gamma 0 left-parenthesis upper N right-parenthesis right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>f</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>z</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:munderover>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ∑\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                ∞\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                            </mml:munderover>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>a</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>f</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>q</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ∈\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msubsup>\n                              <mml:mi>S</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>k</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mtext>new</mml:mtext>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msubsup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                Γ\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(z)=\\sum _{n=1}^\\infty a_f(n)q^n\\in S^{\\text {new}}_k (\\Gamma _0(N))</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    be a newform with squarefree level\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper N\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    that does not have complex multiplication. For a prime\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    , define\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"theta Subscript p Baseline element-of left-bracket 0 comma pi right-bracket\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                θ\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ∈\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\theta _p\\in [0,\\pi ]</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    to be the angle for which\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a Subscript f Baseline left-parenthesis p right-parenthesis equals 2 p Superscript left-parenthesis k minus 1 right-parenthesis slash 2 Baseline cosine theta Subscript p\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>a</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>f</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>k</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  −\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mo>/</mml:mo>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mi>cos</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                θ\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_f(p)=2p^{( k -1)/2}\\cos \\theta _p</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    . Let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper I subset-of left-bracket 0 comma pi right-bracket\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>I</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⊂\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset [0,\\pi ]</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    be a closed subinterval, and let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"d mu Subscript upper S upper T Baseline equals StartFraction 2 Over pi EndFraction sine squared theta d theta\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>d</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                μ\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>S</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>T</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo>=</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mfrac>\n                              <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                π\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mfrac>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>sin</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              θ\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>d</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              θ\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d\\mu _{ST}=\\frac {2}{\\pi }\\sin ^2\\theta d\\theta</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    be the Sato-Tate measure of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper I\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>I</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    . Assuming that the symmetric power\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>L</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    -functions of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>f</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    satisfy certain analytic properties (all of which follow from Langlands functoriality and the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis), we prove that if\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is sufficiently large, then\n                    <disp-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      \\[\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartAbsoluteValue number-sign StartSet p less-than-or-equal-to x colon theta Subscript p Baseline element-of upper I EndSet minus mu Subscript upper S upper T Baseline left-parenthesis upper I right-parenthesis integral Subscript 2 Superscript x Baseline StartFraction d t Over log t EndFraction EndAbsoluteValue much-less-than StartFraction x Superscript 3 slash 4 Baseline log left-parenthesis upper N k x right-parenthesis Over log x EndFraction\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mo>|</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                #\n                                \n                              </mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ≤\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo>:</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  θ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>p</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ∈\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>I</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                −\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  μ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mi>S</mml:mi>\n                                  <mml:mi>T</mml:mi>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                              </mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>I</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:msubsup>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  ∫\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:msubsup>\n                              <mml:mfrac>\n                                <mml:mrow>\n                                  <mml:mi>d</mml:mi>\n                                  <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mrow>\n                                  <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                                  <mml:mo>\n                                    ⁡\n                                    \n                                  </mml:mo>\n                                  <mml:mi>t</mml:mi>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                              </mml:mfrac>\n                              <mml:mo>|</mml:mo>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ≪\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mfrac>\n                              <mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:msup>\n                                  <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                                  <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                    <mml:mn>3</mml:mn>\n                                    <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                      <mml:mo>/</mml:mo>\n                                    </mml:mrow>\n                                    <mml:mn>4</mml:mn>\n                                  </mml:mrow>\n                                </mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  ⁡\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>k</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  ⁡\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:mfrac>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\left |\\#\\{p\\leq x:\\theta _p\\in I\\} -\\mu _{ST}(I)\\int _2^x\\frac {dt}{\\log t}\\right |\\ll \\frac {x^{3/4}\\log (N k x)}{\\log x}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                      \\]\n                    </disp-formula>\n                    with an implied constant of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3.33\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mn>3.33</mml:mn>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.33</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    . By letting\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper I\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>I</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    be a short interval centered at\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 2 EndFraction\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mfrac>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              π\n                              \n                            </mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                          </mml:mfrac>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac {\\pi }{2}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    and counting the primes using a smooth cutoff, we compute a lower bound for the density of positive integers\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    for which\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a Subscript f Baseline left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis not-equals 0\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>a</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>f</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ≠\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_f(n)\\neq 0</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    . In particular, if\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"tau\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>\n                            τ\n                            \n                          </mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is the Ramanujan tau function, then under the aforementioned hypotheses, we prove that\n                    <disp-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      \\[\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"limit Underscript x right-arrow normal infinity Endscripts StartFraction number-sign StartSet n less-than-or-equal-to x colon tau left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis not-equals 0 EndSet Over x EndFraction greater-than 1 minus 1.54 times 10 Superscript negative 13 Baseline period\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:munder>\n                              <mml:mo movablelimits=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">lim</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">\n                                  →\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                  ∞\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:munder>\n                            <mml:mfrac>\n                              <mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                  #\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  ≤\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>:</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  τ\n                                  \n                                </mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  ≠\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>0</mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mml:mo>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mfrac>\n                            <mml:mo>&gt;</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              −\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1.54</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ×\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mn>10</mml:mn>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  −\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>13</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo>.</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lim _{x\\to \\infty }\\frac {\\#\\{n\\leq x:\\tau (n)\\neq 0\\}}{x}&gt;1-1.54\\times 10^{-13}.</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                      \\]\n                    </disp-formula>\n                    We also discuss the connection between the density of positive integers\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    for which\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a Subscript f Baseline left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis not-equals 0\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>a</mml:mi>\n                      